\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A coordinate conditional law at fixed connection}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{For the fixed connection of \ref{fdip-0077}, choose orthonormal
retained and eliminated coordinates and write
##{Q_U=\begin{pmatrix}A_U&B_U\\B_U^T&C_U\end{pmatrix},\qquad C_U>0.}
The basis map sends those ordered frames to the blocks of this
matrix. The retained precision at that connection is
#{A_U-B_UC_U^{-1}B_U^T}, and
##{\phi_{\mathrm{elim}}\mid(\phi_{\mathrm{ret}}=x,U)
 \sim N(-C_U^{-1}B_U^Tx,C_U^{-1}).}
The connection remains part of the conditioning data.}
